Feature: Checkout Payment Regression
  As an e-commerce customer
  I want my card payment, promo discount, and order status to remain consistent through checkout
  So that I am never charged incorrectly or left with a confirmed order that was not actually paid for

  Background:
    Given the customer has items in the cart and a valid checkout session
    And a sandbox test card is configured for payment

  @smoke @critical @risk-critical
  Scenario: Order is not confirmed when stock depletes during in-progress payment authorization
    Given the customer has added the last available unit of a product to the cart
    And the customer has submitted payment authorization with a valid test card
    When stock for that product is depleted by a concurrent order before capture completes
    Then the order status is not "confirmed"
    And the order status matches the gateway's authorization outcome (both report the payment as not captured)

  @regression @risk-high
  Scenario: Captured amount matches cart total after promo code recalculation
    Given the customer has applied a valid promo code that reduces the cart total to a discounted amount
    When the customer completes payment authorization and capture
    Then the gateway authorization amount equals the discounted cart total exactly

  @boundary @edge-case @risk-high
  Scenario: Captured amount is correctly rounded when promo discount produces a fractional sub-unit amount
    Given the promo-discounted cart total produces an amount with more decimal places than the currency's smallest unit
    When the customer submits payment authorization
    Then the captured amount matches the displayed cart total to the currency's smallest unit with no rounding discrepancy

  @negative @security @risk-high
  Scenario: CVV is not exposed when a card payment is declined
    Given the customer submits a card payment using a test card configured to be declined by the sandbox gateway
    When the payment authorization is declined
    Then the error response returned to the client contains no raw CVV value
    And any card number shown in the response or logs is masked to first 6 and last 4 digits only

  @regression @risk-high
  Scenario: Duplicate webhook callback does not alter a confirmed order's status
    Given the payment gateway has already sent a successful payment webhook for an order and the order status is "confirmed"
    When the identical webhook callback is redelivered a second time with the same payment reference
    Then the order status remains "confirmed" with no additional status transition recorded

  @regression @data-driven @risk-medium
  Scenario Outline: Invalid or expired promo codes are rejected without changing the cart total
    Given the customer enters promo code "<input>" at checkout
    When the customer applies the promo code to the cart
    Then the system responds with "<expected>"
    And the cart total remains at its pre-promo amount

    Examples:
      | input       | expected                       |
      | EXPIRED2023 | promo code expired              |
      | ABC#$%123   | promo code invalid format        |
      | NOTEXIST99  | promo code not recognized        |

